"Assume that $\\dim(\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}})=d$. Let\n\n$$\nh=\\sum_{C\\in\\mathcal{C}(G)}h_{\\mathcal{X}_C,y_C}.\n$$\n\nLet $\\sigma$ be the subdivision of $\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}}$ induced by $h$, and let $\\sigma_C$ be the subdivision of $\\pi_C(\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}})$ induced by $h_{\\mathcal{X}_C,y_C}$. For $z\\in\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}}$, let $k_z$ and $l_z$ be the codimensions of the minimal faces of $\\sigma$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}}$ containing $z$, respectively. For each $C\\in\\mathcal{C}(G)$, let $k_{z,C}$ and $l_{z,C}$ be the codimensions of the minimal faces of $\\sigma_C$ and $\\pi_C(\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}})$ containing $z_C$, respectively.\n\n**Generic codimension additivity conjecture.** If $\\mathcal{S}_{G,\\mathcal{X}}$ and all tent functions $h_{\\mathcal{X}_C,y_C}$ are sufficiently generic, then\n\n$$\nk_z-l_z=\\sum_{C\\in\\mathcal{C}(G)}k_{z,C}-\\sum_{C\\in\\mathcal{C}(G)}l_{z,C}.\n$$\n\nThe preceding corollary proves only the corresponding inequality for the subdivision codimensions. The generic equality is presented as a conjectural strengthening and concerns the combinatorics of intersections of clique-wise regular subdivisions."